            "content": "<p><strong>Common bundle patterns are highly seasonal and store-specific.</strong> In Zava Retail Redmond, the top co-purchased pair changes every season, but the <em>bundle frequency is consistently low</em>: most leading pairs appear only <strong>2 times</strong> per season, with shares typically between <strong>0.88%</strong> and <strong>1.71%</strong> of orders.</p><ul><li><strong>Highest bundle share:</strong> <em>Lineman's Pliers 9-inch + Needle-Nose Pliers 6-inch</em> in <strong>Spring 2022</strong>, appearing <strong>3 times</strong> across <strong>175 orders</strong> for a <strong>1.71%</strong> share.</li><li><strong>Other strong bundles:</strong> <em>Toilet Repair Kit Complete + Plumber's Grease</em> in <strong>Winter 2024</strong> reached <strong>3 of 204 orders</strong> (<strong>1.47%</strong>), and <em>Ball Peen Hammer 12oz + Pipe Wrench Set</em> in <strong>Summer 2021</strong> reached <strong>2 of 139 orders</strong> (<strong>1.44%</strong>).</li><li><strong>Lowest bundle share in the table:</strong> <em>Ball Peen Hammer 12oz + Finishing Hammer 13oz</em> in <strong>Spring 2026</strong> at <strong>2 of 228 orders</strong> (<strong>0.88%</strong>).</li></ul><p><strong>Seasonal buying behavior differs meaningfully.</strong> Across all eligible orders, volume rises over time from <strong>652 orders in 2020</strong> to <strong>897 in 2026</strong>, while line items increase from <strong>1,361</strong> to <strong>1,828</strong>. Seasonal order counts are strongest in <strong>winter</strong> and <strong>spring</strong> in later years: for example, <strong>Winter 2026</strong> had <strong>232 orders</strong> and <strong>479 line items</strong>, versus <strong>Summer 2026</strong> with <strong>218 orders</strong> and <strong>427 line items</strong>.</p><p><strong>Interpretation:</strong> Redmond\u2019s bundles suggest customers often buy complementary tools or project-specific items together, but no single bundle dominates. The strongest seasonal signals are practical: plumbing and repair items in winter, electrical and insulation items in spring/fall, and outdoor/garden or power-tool combinations in summer. This points to <em>project-driven purchasing</em> rather than broad cross-season bundle loyalty.</p>",
